{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>For not like our Rock is their rock.</b> The words of Moses, meaning: a nation devoid of counsel. And the sense is: for our Rock sold us, and they have no rock like our Rock, nor are they better than Him. And likewise it says: \"and our enemies are not judges\" etc., like \"and I have not learned wisdom\" etc. And some say that it is thus: \"and our enemies will acknowledge it.\" Therefore it is not joined with \"the vine of Sodom.\""], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:06.916163020Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}